================================================================================
1. PRODUCT MISSION & BACKGROUND
================================================================================

Background & The Industry Dilemma:
Refineries, Public Sector Undertakings (PSUs), defence-linked manufacturing
units, and government offices generate substantial volumes of routine but
highly sensitive knowledge work:
- Formal approval notes and board presentations
- Engineering calculations and design reviews
- Source code for internal utilities and SCADA systems
- Review of scanned engineering drawings (P&IDs), inspection reports, and SOPs

None of this confidential work can be processed through public cloud AI
assistants (such as Claude, ChatGPT, or GitHub Copilot) because the underlying
data is classified and business-critical:
- Piping & Instrument Diagrams (P&IDs)
- Proprietary financials and tender/vendor negotiations
- Unreleased military/industrial designs
- Internal correspondence, audits, and strategic notes

Company policies strictly mandate that this data remain strictly on-premises.
As a result, organizations face an unacceptable compromise: either staff perform
these tedious tasks manually (sacrificing massive productivity gains), or
employees quietly leak confidential data into public cloud tools to get work done.

Open-weight reasoning and vision models have reached the capability threshold
needed to power a genuinely useful enterprise assistant. However, off-the-shelf
deployable solutions tailored for industrial, air-gapped environments simply do
not exist. Snap solves this problem.


================================================================================
2. SYSTEM DESCRIPTION: THE AIR-GAPPED AI WORKBENCH
================================================================================

Snap delivers a self-hosted, sovereign AI workbench running entirely on
the organization's own GPU server hardware. Zero external calls are made;
nothing ever leaves the premises.

Key Pillars of the System:

1. Dynamic Multi-Model Auto-Selection:
   The backend is never locked to a single monolithic model. It concurrently
   hosts multiple open-weight models and automatically routes requests to the
   ideal specialist:
   - Coding tasks -> dispatched to specialized code LLMs (e.g., Qwen-Coder)
   - Complex reasoning -> dispatched to deep reasoning models (e.g., Gemma/DeepSeek)
   - Routine text & summaries -> dispatched to fast general-purpose models
   - Scanned PDFs & drawings -> dispatched to multimodal vision/OCR models
   New open-weight models can be registered and hot-swapped without redesigning
   the system architecture.

2. Full Agentic Execution & Extensible Tool Ecosystem:
   Rather than acting as a simple one-shot conversational bot, the system acts
   as an autonomous agent:
   - Native, pre-included Model Context Protocol (MCP) support enabled via
     '--webui-mcp-proxy' for seamless, standardized local tool integration
   - Actively introducing an expanded on-premises tool suite: local file I/O
     (read/write), spreadsheet manipulation, internal search, and sandboxed
     code execution
   - Plans multi-step execution paths and iterates until deliverables meet
     organizational requirements

3. Deep Multimodal Understanding & Document QA:
   The system currently features active partial document reading and QA
   capabilities (detecting uploaded PDFs and image payloads, extracting text,
   and routing to vision models). This foundation is actively expanding to
   process complex, messy industrial artifacts:
   - Reading and answering questions across multi-page PDF inspection reports
   - Handwritten engineering shift logs, maintenance records, and site notes
   - Technical blueprints, schematics, and P&ID diagrams
   - High-resolution photographic site inspections

4. Tangible Deliverables (Not Just Chat):
   Generates production-grade business and engineering assets:
   - Ready-to-circulate approval notes
   - Standard Microsoft Office files (.docx, .xlsx, .pptx)
   - Tested, verified internal code utilities
   - Step-by-step engineering calculations with formula derivations

5. Local Grounding (Zero-Leakage Knowledge Base):
   Connects to on-premises manuals, standard operating procedures (SOPs),
   regulations, and historical correspondence via a local vector/document index,
   ensuring hallucination-free outputs without external API calls.

6. High-Performance llama.cpp Core (Speculative Decoding & Quantization):
   Built natively on llama.cpp, the workbench achieves state-of-the-art inference
   throughput on organizational GPU/CPU hardware:
   - Speculative Decoding: Pairs a lightweight draft model with a larger target
     model to generate multiple candidate tokens in parallel, significantly
     accelerating inference speed and reducing latency per token without loss
     of generation quality.
   - Advanced GGUF Quantization: Supports modern 4-bit, 5-bit, and 8-bit quantization
     formats (e.g., Q4_K_M, Q5_K_M, Q8_0), enabling massive 70B+ parameter
     reasoning and coding models to fit comfortably within available VRAM and
     run with peak computational efficiency.

   Why llama.cpp?
   - Architectural Excellence & Battle-Tested Reliability: Rather than building
     a bespoke inference engine that merely 'just works', Snap builds upon a
     phenomenal, production-grade, and mature C/C++ architecture. If an open-source
     system is already extraordinarily well-engineered, battle-tested, and actively
     optimized by top systems engineers globally, adopting it ensures rock-solid
     reliability and peak performance rather than maintaining a fragile, reinvented
     wheel.
   - 100% Open-Source & Sovereign Integrity: Fully open-weight and open-source with
     zero proprietary locks, zero telemetry, and zero remote call-homes. This is
     paramount for strict air-gapped refineries, PSUs, and defence environments.
   - Bare-Metal Hardware Extraction: Highly optimized compute kernels (CUDA, Metal,
     ROCm, Vulkan, AVX-512) and memory-mapped (mmap) file loading allow organizations
     to extract every ounce of performance from their existing server hardware.


